# AgentForge permanent constraints

## Architecture

- Control plane and execution plane stay separated. Trusted apps orchestrate; they never sandboxes or shells.
- NEVER execute user-supplied code, commands, scripts, or task bundles in the trusted control plane (`apps/web`, shared TS packages).
- Task versions are immutable once published. Create a new version instead of mutating.
- Database tenancy is org-scoped. Queries and policies must include organization boundaries.
- Validate schemas (Zod / contracts) at every trust boundary — HTTP, queue payloads, adapter I/O.
- Supabase service role is server-only. Never expose it to client bundles or `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`.
- Benchmark, model, agent, and sandbox integrations go behind adapters (`BenchmarkAdapter`, `ModelProvider`, `AgentAdapter`, `SandboxProvider`, `ArtifactStore`, `JobQueue`, `EnvironmentAdapter`, `CiCheckAdapter`).

## Engineering

- No unnecessary dependencies. Prefer stdlib / existing workspace packages.
- Strict TypeScript. No `any`. Prefer branded IDs and Zod inference.
- Do not claim done without running relevant tests (unit at minimum; Playwright smoke when UI changes).
- Update docs/ADRs when architecture changes.
- Accessibility and design-system tokens matter. Use `@agentforge/ui` primitives; avoid ad-hoc purple SaaS aesthetics.
- Do not implement billing, Kafka, Kubernetes, ClickHouse, or invented scores unless explicitly requested.
- Harbor, sandboxes, and training run only in `services/evaluator` and `services/training`. Never in `apps/web` or shared TS packages.
